Yes, that's why you have to lure him up usually at least two levels.
(Luring him up is more reliable than luring him down, because it
doesn't require beating him to the stairs.)  Once you get him to a
level that allows teleport, you can do the following:

 1. Wait until he shows up to "attack" (i.e., pester) you.
 2. Teleport to the up stairs.
 3. Now he will come to you.  Yay.
 4. Whack him with your favorite weapon, repeatedly.
 5. He will escape to the level below.
 6. Teleport to the down stairs.  Go down.
 7. If this level also allows teleport, repeat from step 1.
 (If not, you don't want him fleeing down again,
  because you can't teleport to those stairs.)
 8. Step off the up stair (but stay next to it).
 9. He will come stand on the up stair.
10. Whack him once, and he'll escape up.
11. Go up.  Now you are on a level that allows teleport.
12. Repeat from step 1.

I usually have to go through this cycle about three times before he
finally keels over.

It works, but it's annoying to have to tediously lure him up past d5
non-teleport demon lairs to finally get to a level where you can
teleport.  Non-teleport levels suck, and Gehennom's full of them,
often directly adjacent to one another, which is really annoying.  I
think the worst configuration is Medusa on DL27, Castle on 28, Valley
on 29, Jubilex and Baalzebub on 30 and 31 (either order), Asmodeus on
32, Orcus on 33, a total of SEVEN consecutive non-teleport levels.  I
don't think I've ever had it quite that bad, but I have certainly had
three or four non-teleport levels consecutively, and it sucks.  At
least they don't all have undiggable walls and floors.  (Wait, don't
tell me:  in Slash'em they do, right?)


